  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.1.0 — New option `NeverStepUpCategories`: Serilog `SourceContext` prefixes the step-up never raises above `BaseLevel`, defaulting to `[\"Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Database.Command\"]`. Observable behaviour change: EF Core SQL commands (logged at `Information`) are no longer exported during a step-up window by default — a DB-backed service no longer floods its telemetry with unredacted SQL for `DurationSeconds` after every error. `Warning`/`Error` events in a listed category still export (the category is pinned to `BaseLevel`, not silenced); matching is ordinal on an exact or `prefix.`-delimited `SourceContext`; the list has no effect in `AlwaysOn` mode; and the pre-error buffer is deliberately not filtered, so buffered SQL still flushes on error. Set `\"NeverStepUpCategories\": []` to restore v3.0.0 behaviour. No public API break.",
